        penwidth=1.4;
        margin=18;

        S1 [label="State", shape="ellipse", fillcolor="#A9DDB0", color="#4F9A5C"];
        A1 [label="Action", shape="box", style="filled,rounded", fillcolor="#FFC98A", color="#D98E2B"];
        R1 [label="Reward", shape="diamond", fillcolor="#9CC4F2", color="#1565C0"];

        S1 -> A1 [label="  policy  π₁", fontcolor="#4A4A4A"];
        A1 -> R1 [label="  dynamics", fontcolor="#4A4A4A"];
        S1 -> R1 [style="dashed", color="#8C8C8C", constraint="false"];
    }

    subgraph cluster_env2 {
        label="Environment 2";
        fontname="Helvetica-Bold";
        fontsize=13;
        fontcolor="#1A1A2E";
        style="rounded,filled";
        fillcolor="#F7F9FC";
        color="#B8C4D9";
        penwidth=1.4;
        margin=18;

        S2 [label="State", shape="ellipse", fillcolor="#A9DDB0", color="#4F9A5C"];
        A2 [label="Action", shape="box", style="filled,rounded", fillcolor="#FFC98A", color="#D98E2B"];
        R2 [label="Reward", shape="diamond", fillcolor="#9CC4F2", color="#1565C0"];

        S2 -> A2 [label="  policy  π₂", fontcolor="#4A4A4A"];
        A2 -> R2 [label="  dynamics", fontcolor="#4A4A4A"];
        S2 -> R2 [style="dashed", color="#8C8C8C", constraint="false"];
    }

    { rank=same; S1; S2; }
    { rank=same; A1; A2; }
    { rank=same; R1; R2; }

    S1 -> S2 [style=invis];
    R1 -> R2 [style=invis];

    A1 -> A2 [
        label="  knowledge transfer  ",
        style="bold",
        color="#B23A48",
        fontcolor="#B23A48",
        penwidth=2.2
    ];
}
```
::::
:::

- **Causal Approach**: Transfer depends on which mechanisms are shared
  - Let $\mathcal{G}_1, \mathcal{G}_2$ be causal graphs for
    $\mathcal{E}_1, \mathcal{E}_2$
  - Policy $\pi^*$ transfers if causal mechanisms of action on reward are
    _identical_:
    $$f_r^{(1)}(a, s, s') = f_r^{(2)}(a, s, s')$$
  - Even if distributions shift: $\Pr^{(1)}(s) \neq \Pr^{(2)}(s)$

- **Formal Criterion**: _Transportability_ (Pearl & Bareinboim)
  - Check graph structure, not surface similarity
  - Answerable before deployment

* Causal RL: Open Challenges

\begingroup \scriptsize
| **Challenge** | **What it is** | **Why it matters** |
|----------|----------|----------| 
| **Causal Discovery** | Learn graph $\mathcal{G}$ from interaction data | Lack of known causal structure; partial observability complicates discovery |
| **Identifiability** | Multiple SCMs yield identical observational distribution | Risk recovering wrong causal graph; interventions needed but costly |
| **Scalability** | Integrate causal structure into deep RL | Current methods don't scale to high-dim state spaces; risk losing features |
| **Sample Efficiency** | Necessary causal knowledge for robustness | Open question: complete graph vs. partial knowledge vs. statistical approximation |
| **Partial Observability** | Agent observes limited state; hidden variables affect action and reward | Confounding hides in unobserved state; deconfounding harder |
\endgroup

- **Key Open Question**: Can you learn enough causal structure online to improve
  generalization and robustness without full causal discovery cost?
